      "narrative": "The Copper Finch is quiet for this hour\u2014just the sullen glow of the lamps and the scratch of a match against stone. Mara Venn turns from where she leans against the bar, her charcoal coat creaking as she sizes you up. She's about to speak when Toran Vex, the ink-stained clerk nursing a cup at the next table, cuts in first.\n\n\"Ash Gate? *I'm* the one who kept that lock turning for eight years. She doesn't know the half of it.\"\n\nMara gives him a flat look, then shrugs at you. \"He's not wrong. Toran's the lockwright. Sworn to the Kestrel Guild and all that.\"\n\nYou step closer, ready to press for details\u2014but the words tangle the moment you open your mouth. You ask about the lock's mechanism, about Old Bram, about who ordered it sealed, but the questions come out jumbled, one tripping over the next. Toran's brow furrows. He tilts his head.\n\n\"...You alright there? You're asking like you've already decided the answer.\"\n\nMara's eyes narrow. She doesn't answer your question. Instead, she gives you a long, slow look, then turns back to her drink.\n\n\"You're not making much sense, friend. Maybe sit down, catch your breath. Toran\u2014didn't you have that ledger to finish?\"\n\nToran blinks, clearly thrown by the shift. \"I\u2014yes. Yes, I should\u2014\" He gathers his papers, shooting you an odd, uncertain glance as he does.\n\nNeither of them has told you a thing. And now Mara's gone quiet, sipping her ale with the deliberate patience of someone who's decided to wait and see what you do next.\n\nThe copper lamps hiss overhead. The morning rain taps at the shutters.\n\nWhat do you do?"
    },
