      "narrative": "You take a breath, slow down, and this time you phrase the question cleanly\u2014*who was the lockwright before the gate was sealed?*\n\nMara Venn sets her ale down. She studies you for a moment\u2014a reassessment\u2014then nods once, as if you've passed some small test.\n\n\"Before Toran? That'd be the one who trained him. A woman named **Sable Quill**.\" She says the name like she's testing how it lands. \"She was the Kestrel Guild's senior lockwright for the Ash Gate for close to fifteen years. Knew every pin, every ward, every rust-scar in that mechanism.\"\n\nShe leans forward, voice dropping.\n\n\"She's still alive, far as I know. But she's not here\u2014she's out at the gate itself. Has a little alcove she works out of, just north of the arch. Keeps to herself, doesn't come into town much. If anyone knows *why* that lock was filed\u2014not just maintained, but *filed*\u2014it'd be her.\"\n\nShe picks her ale back up, watching you over the rim.\n\n\"Course, she might not talk to a stranger. She's Guild, through and through. But that's your lead, if you want it.\"\n\nThe name hangs in the air. **Sable Quill.** The lockwright who came before. Still at the gate."
    },
